  "regressions": [
    "Running entity callbacks remain registered until their call and inline completion chain return, even if their future has already completed or was cancelled.",
    "Re-enable requires the prior SQL worker, entity callbacks and inventory pipelines to finish.",
    "Fatal errors complete the asynchronous result and release dependent guards before propagating to the worker/server error handler.",
    "A worker failing with AssertionError still drains the next already-accepted transaction during shutdown.",
    "SQL submission captures one generation and one executor; it cannot switch to a later lifecycle worker after its admission check.",
    "Inventory pipeline startup releases its per-player guard for synchronous Error as well as RuntimeException.",
    "Ordinary shutdown-hook and linkage failures are logged independently; a finally block still drains the SQL worker."
  ],
